  "details": "TLDR: My goal is to add Audio source shapes to the list of components world makers can use to allow for much more immersive audio in worlds\nAs a professional level designer I always aim to give the best, most immersive experiences through atmosphere and surroundings. however one struggle I always run into when designing worlds for vrchat is audio. Audio is so vastly important to selling a rich and full gaming experience, however Unitys default audio engine leaves a lot to be desired. As someone who uses unity for many other things outside of vrchat, one thing I always use is a paid addon made by Carlos Wilkes called Volumetric Audio.\nWhat Volumetric Audio aims to do is allow the world creator to alter the base emission shape of an audio source to other shapes outside of the default point shape. For example a world creator could put two rooms next to each other and have two separate square audio sources that dont leak into the surrounding rooms. It also allows for many other Incredibly immersive features like Volumetric Reverb Zones, Mesh Baking, and Audio Occlusion so things like closing a door could stop the audio from leaving a room. This Unity package offers many new tools that would help world makers create places that seem much more dynamic and alive\nVolumetric Audio is a standalone addon that I am requesting to be added to the whitelist of usable scripted components like dynamic bones. Below is the link to the package on the unity assets store\nhttps://assetstore.unity.com/packages/tools/audio/volumetric-audio-17125",
